# Pipeline-generated output (regenerated every run; authoritative copy lives on the
# `data-sync` branch, which is Vercel's Production Branch). Committing these to `main`
# caused a real production incident: main's copy went stale and Vercel's Git
# integration deployed it, silently overriding fresher CLI/data-sync deploys. See
# PROJECT_REVIEW.md DEV-27. The booster collation overlay is generated weekly on the
# `collation-metadata` branch and fetched by the daily workflow before simulation.
# Hand-maintained config (product_overrides.json) and non-pipeline static data
# (precon_decks.json, booster_slots.json, scryfall_set_hierarchy.json) are NOT
# ignored and must stay tracked.
public/data/booster_collation_overrides.json
public/data/sets.json
public/data/sealed_products.json
public/data/booster_ev.json
public/data/arbitrage_leaderboard.json
public/data/product_metrics.json
public/data/single_card_prices.json
public/data/pricing_reliability.json
public/data/product_chase_cards.json
public/data/pipeline_execution_logs.json
public/data/latest_pipeline_run.json
public/data/mtg.sqlite
